     'how_en' => 'Heat load (BTU/hr) = area × base load × (ceiling height ÷ 10) × sun factor + 600 BTU for each person beyond two. Tons = BTU ÷ 12,000, rounded up to the next half ton (minimum 0.75 ton). This is a rule of thumb for Indian summers.',
